    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen `ui2` and `nohlsearch` are enabled, the highlight that allows you to locate which selection is getting replaced for the find/replace confirmation fails to render.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun `nvim --clean -u minimal.lua` with `minimal.lua`:\n\n```lua\nrequire('vim._core.ui2').enable({\n\tenable = true,\n\tmsg = {\n\t\ttargets = 'cmd',\n\t\tcmd = {\n\t\t\theight = 0.5,\n\t\t},\n\t\tdialog = {\n\t\t\theight = 0.5,\n\t\t},\n\t\tmsg = {\n\t\t\theight = 0.5,\n\t\t\ttimeout = 4000,\n\t\t},\n\t\tpager = {\n\t\t\theight = 0.999,\n\t\t},\n\t},\n})\n\nvim.opt.hlsearch = false\n```\nThen use the find/replace with confirmation command (`%s/te/t/gc`) on a test file with the characters `te` like this:\n```markdown\n# Heading 1\n## Heading 2\n### Heading 3\n\nsome text\n\ntesting\n```\n\nThe highlight appears when typing out the command, but once it enters the `confirmation` mode, the highlights all disappear.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe characters to be replaced should be highlighted. (no `ui2` only `nohlsearch`)\n\n<img width=\"968\" height=\"1170\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5508ab95-6582-4572-8d79-ddbb262e9b17\" />\n\nActual behavior:\n\n<img width=\"968\" height=\"1170\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc61a33f-05c6-4f4d-a601-b86485ff1774\" />\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1156+g635acc7dc8 Build type: RelWithDebInfo LuaJIT 2.1.1785005726\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nPop!_OS 22.04\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty 0.16.0-dev\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
